args.command:
node -e '
// Check forces at s=26.5 in HOLD with maxDownforceKg = 600 vs 4700
// Wait: on a concave curve, the front wheel normal n_F and rear wheel normal n_R differ by angle 2*a/R!
// And tireFwd at the front wheel is t_F (pointing up-left), while at the rear wheel it is t_R!
// Notice that t_F + t_R has an OUTWARD (-N) component of 2 * sin(a/R) * Flong!
// When Flong > 0 (driving forward up a concave curve), the front and rear tires pushing along the tangent of a concave curve produce a component pressing INTO the curve of Flong * (a/R), PLUS the chord geometry!
console.log("Chord sagitta a^2 / (2R) =", (1.38*1.38 / (2 * 12)).toFixed(4), "m");
'

